title: Require authorization to revoke mobile relay bindings
---
B111 found that DELETE /binding/<binding_id> reaches mobile binding revocation through a self-auth bypass. The handler validates only binding-ID shape, then removes a matching binding and exposes existence; no bearer credential, Ed25519 proof, or binding-owner proof is required.

Acceptance criteria:
- Require a proof bound to the machine or phone key that created the binding, or a narrowly scoped revocation credential.
- A bare binding ID must not authorize deletion or disclose binding existence.
- Add token-configured integration tests proving anonymous revocation is rejected and an authorized owner can revoke.
- Keep the live validation non-destructive; do not test against production bindings.

Evidence: B111 audit.